{"name":"Borg Drone","hex":"#06470c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"borg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of cyborg."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative spelling of Borg."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/borg"},{"term":"drone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male hymenopteran (ant, bee, hornet, or wasp), whose sole primary function is to mate with the queen.","One who does not work; a lazy person, an idler."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To kill or destroy with a drone (unmanned aircraft), or with a missile fired by a drone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Borg","blocks":[{"text":"The Borg are an alien group that appear as recurring antagonists in the Star Trek fictional universe. They are cyborgs linked in a hive mind called \"The Collective\". The Borg co-opted the technology and knowledge of other alien species to the Collective through the process of \"assimilation\": forcibly transforming individual beings into \"drones\" by injecting nanoprobes into their bodies and surgically augmenting them with cybernetic components. The Borg's ultimate goal is \"achieving perfection\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borg"},{"title":"Drone (Star Trek: Voyager)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Drone\" is the 96th episode of the science fiction television series Star Trek: Voyager, the second episode of the fifth season. The crew of the 24th-century spacecraft USS Voyager deal with a Borg drone, played by guest star J. Paul Boehmer."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drone_(Star_Trek%3A_Voyager)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Borg_dockingstation.jpg/500px-Borg_dockingstation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Borg_dockingstation.jpg/1280px-Borg_dockingstation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Borg_dockingstation.jpg/500px-Borg_dockingstation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An occupied Borg \"alcove\" prop on display at the Hollywood Entertainment Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABorg_dockingstation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a1/Picard_as_Locutus.jpg/330px-Picard_as_Locutus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a1/Picard_as_Locutus.jpg/330px-Picard_as_Locutus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Patrick Stewart as Locutus of Borg, the assimilated Jean-Luc Picard","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APicard_as_Locutus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bc/Borg_Queen_2372.jpg/250px-Borg_Queen_2372.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bc/Borg_Queen_2372.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bc/Borg_Queen_2372.jpg/250px-Borg_Queen_2372.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alice Krige as the Borg Queen in Star Trek: First Contact","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABorg_Queen_2372.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Susanna_Thompson_at_PaleyFest_2013.jpg/500px-Susanna_Thompson_at_PaleyFest_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Susanna_Thompson_at_PaleyFest_2013.jpg/500px-Susanna_Thompson_at_PaleyFest_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna